---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { APK_URL, formatDate } from '../i18n';
import { releases } from '../releases';
import Screenshots from '../components/Screenshots.astro';
import CarAudio from '../components/CarAudio.astro';

// The newest release, shown under the download button.
const [latest] = await releases('en');
---
<Page lang="en" page="index" title='CastBay: AirPlay Receiver for Android TVs, Cars and Tablets – Mirror Your iPhone' description='Free, open-source app that turns an Android TV, TV box, car display or tablet into an AirPlay receiver: mirror your iPhone, iPad or Mac, play music with lyrics, and cast video. DLNA too.'>
<main>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow slogan">Cast it, it's there. Kick back with CastBay.</p>
      <h1>
        Cast your iPhone to your Android screen
      </h1>
      <p class="lead">
        CastBay lets an Android TV, car display or tablet receive AirPlay screen mirroring, music and video, and the cast button in video and music apps (DLNA). Free, open source, no ads.
      </p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href={APK_URL}>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 3v12m0 0-5-5m5 5 5-5M4 19h16"/></svg>Download APK
        </a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="https://github.com/weenas/castbay">View source
        </a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="#car-audio">In-car music</a>
      </div>
      <p class="note">
        Version {latest.data.version} · {formatDate('en', latest.data.date)} · <a href="/changelog">What's new</a><br>
        For Android TVs, TV boxes, car displays and tablets on Android 6.0 or later
      </p>
      <p class="channels">
        Also on: <a href="https://github.com/weenas/castbay/releases">GitHub releases</a> · <a href="https://apps.obtainium.imranr.dev/redirect?r=obtainium://add/https://github.com/weenas/castbay">Obtainium</a> · F-Droid (under review) · <a href="/faq#where-can-i-get-castbay-and-can-i-switch-between-sources">What's the difference?</a>
      </p>
      <div class="chips">
        <span class="chip">Screen mirroring</span>
        <span class="chip">Music &amp; lyrics</span>
        <span class="chip">Video casting</span>
        <span class="chip">DLNA</span>
        <span class="chip">H.265 · 4K</span>
        <span class="chip">English &amp; Chinese</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="features">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>Everything casting to a TV should be</h2>
        <p>Designed for the big screen, with a remote or a touch screen: mirroring, music and video each get a screen made for them.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid">
        <article class="card">
          <div class="icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="2" y="4" width="20" height="13" rx="2"/><path d="M8 21h8M12 17v4"/></svg></div>
          <h3>Screen mirroring</h3>
          <p>Mirror an iPhone, iPad or Mac in real time at up to 60 fps, and in 4K with H.265 on 4K TVs with hardware HEVC decoding.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <div class="icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M9 18V5l12-2v13"/><circle cx="6" cy="18" r="3"/><circle cx="18" cy="16" r="3"/></svg></div>
          <h3>Music</h3>
          <p>A blurred-cover backdrop, optional scrolling lyrics and playback controls. Supports ALAC audio reception over AirPlay; the actual format and sound quality depend on the sender and audio output path. <a href="#car-audio">Explore in-car music and audio quality</a>.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <div class="icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="2" y="5" width="20" height="14" rx="2"/><path d="m10 9 5 3-5 3z"/></svg></div>
          <h3>Video casting</h3>
          <p>When an app casts a video, the TV plays it straight from the source, so your phone is free. Switch audio tracks and subtitles.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <div class="icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M2 8.5a15 15 0 0 1 20 0M5.5 12a10 10 0 0 1 13 0M9 15.5a5 5 0 0 1 6 0"/><circle cx="12" cy="19" r="1.2" fill="currentColor"/></svg></div>
          <h3>Apps' cast button (DLNA)</h3>
          <p>The cast button in apps like Bilibili, iQiyi, NetEase Cloud Music and QQ Music casts straight to CastBay, from iPhone and Android phones alike.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <div class="icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="7" y="2" width="10" height="20" rx="5"/><circle cx="12" cy="8" r="2"/><path d="M12 14v3"/></svg></div>
          <h3>Remote or touch screen</h3>
          <p>Press Down on the remote while playing, or tap a touch screen, for the quick menu: picture fit, playback stats (for mirroring, the phone's frame rate and network too), audio and subtitles, and for videos pause and skip. A steering wheel's media buttons pause and change tracks. Back twice ends a cast.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <div class="icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 3 4 6v6c0 5 3.5 8 8 9 4.5-1 8-4 8-9V6z"/><path d="m9 12 2 2 4-4"/></svg></div>
          <h3>Private by design</h3>
          <p>Choose who can cast: anyone, devices you allow on the TV, a PIN shown on the TV (as on an Apple TV) or a password. Block any device. No account, nothing collected unless you turn it on, fully open source.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CarAudio lang="en" />

  <section id="screens">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>See it on the TV</h2>
        <p>Screenshots from a Sony TV.</p>
      </div>
      <Screenshots lang="en" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="start">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>User guide</h2>
        <p>Three steps to your first cast. Your TV and phone need to be on the same network.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="steps">
        <div class="card step">
          <h3>Install on your TV</h3>
          <p>Download the CastBay APK from GitHub and install it from a USB drive or the TV's file manager.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card step">
          <h3>Open CastBay</h3>
          <p>It starts receiving as soon as it opens, and from then on it's ready whenever the TV turns on.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card step">
          <h3>Cast from your phone</h3>
          <p>On an iPhone, choose Screen Mirroring in Control Center, or tap the AirPlay icon or cast button in an app, then pick "CastBay (your TV's name)".</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top:28px"><a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/guide">Read the full user guide</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="alt">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>Two ways to cast</h2>
        <p>Many apps support both; pick whichever suits you.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ways">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>AirPlay<span class="tag">Any app</span></h3>
          <ul>
            <li>From Control Center's Screen Mirroring, or an app's AirPlay icon</li>
            <li>Mirroring, music and video</li>
            <li>ALAC audio reception; previous and next from the TV</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>DLNA<span class="tag">Apps' cast button</span></h3>
          <ul>
            <li>From the cast button inside video and music apps</li>
            <li>The TV plays it directly; lock your phone or walk away</li>
            <li>Works from iPhone and Android phones</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="faq">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>FAQ</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="faq">
        <details>
          <summary>Which devices are supported?</summary>
          <p>Android devices on Android 6.0 or later: TVs, TV boxes, car displays and tablets, worked with a remote or a touch screen. Tested on Xiaomi (Android 6), TCL (Android 9) and Sony (Android 12) TVs, a Google TV Streamer and a BYD car display; see the <a href="/compatibility">compatibility list</a>.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>How do I install the APK on a TV?</summary>
          <p>Copy the APK to a USB drive, or open it with a file manager on the TV (ES File Explorer, for example). The first time, the TV may ask you to allow installing apps from unknown sources.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>My phone doesn't find CastBay. What now?</summary>
          <p>Make sure the TV and phone are on the same Wi-Fi and CastBay is open, waiting for a connection. Some routers enable "AP isolation", which stops devices finding each other; turn it off in the router's settings. Turning the phone's Wi-Fi off and on can also help.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Does CastBay collect my data?</summary>
          <p>Not unless you choose to. There's no account, no ads and no third-party analytics. Lyrics lookups, problem reports and anonymous usage statistics each send something only once you turn them on, and never names, titles or links in reports and statistics. See the <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.</p>
        </details>
      </div>
      <p class="faq-more"><a href="/faq">All questions: install, connecting, casting, privacy →</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="alt" id="community">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>Open source, and open to you</h2>
        <p>CastBay is open source: your feedback and testing make it work well on more TVs and cars.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid community">
        <a class="card" href="/feedback">
          <div class="icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M21 15a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H7l-4 4V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h14a2 2 0 0 1 2 2z"/></svg></div>
          <h3>Report a problem</h3>
          <p>Report problems and suggest ideas on GitHub. In the app, About → Diagnostics uploads a log in one step: just give its report ID.</p>
          <span class="more">How to give feedback →</span>
        </a>
        <a class="card" href="https://github.com/weenas/castbay">
          <div class="icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="m16 18 6-6-6-6M8 6l-6 6 6 6"/></svg></div>
          <h3>Source code</h3>
          <p>Open source under GPL-3.0, built on UxPlay, libplist, Apple's ALAC decoder and Media3 ExoPlayer. The code, how to build it and every release are on GitHub.</p>
          <span class="more">github.com/weenas/castbay →</span>
        </a>
        <a class="card" href="/compatibility">
          <div class="icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="2" y="4" width="20" height="13" rx="2"/><path d="m9 10.5 2 2 4-4M8 21h8"/></svg></div>
          <h3>Device compatibility</h3>
          <p>Does CastBay work on your TV, box or car? Tell us the model and Android version, and save the next person the guesswork.</p>
          <span class="more">See the compatibility list →</span>
        </a>
        <a class="card" href="/changelog.xml">
          <div class="icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M4 11a9 9 0 0 1 9 9M4 4a16 16 0 0 1 16 16"/><circle cx="5" cy="19" r="1"/></svg></div>
          <h3>Follow updates</h3>
          <p>Subscribe to the changelog by RSS; on a tablet, Obtainium can also follow new releases on GitHub. CastBay on a TV checks for updates itself.</p>
          <span class="more">Subscribe by RSS →</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>
</Page>
